  "case": "wildcards_and_colons/mid_field_question_mark_crossing_a_colon",
  "source": "simulator_check/cases/wildcards_and_colons.json",
  "question": "Can a * in the middle of an ARN segment, or a ?, match a colon, in Resource and in ArnLike? The analyzer assumes not: only a * that ends a segment runs on past colons (review finding F6).",
  "description": "Third follow-up: in us-east-1?111122223333, the ? stands where the alias's ARN has the colon between the region and the account. The pattern still has six colons, so it isn't a short ARN. It matches only if a ? in one of the first five fields can match a colon.",
  "readings": {
    "ALLOW": "a ? in one of the first five fields matches a colon too: Resource is a plain glob over the whole ARN",
    "IMPLICIT_DENY": "it doesn't: in the first five fields, a ? matches one character other than a colon"
  },
